      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "The speedy RADICALS (3) is back for a second campaign. Just missed over this trip at Hawkesbury on debut then led for home but was overwhelmed in her other two runs, also at 1000m. Two recent trials should have her ready to run well. BUNDY BELLE (7) couldn't go the early speed but warmed up late to finish third on debut over 900m at Newcastle last time out. Prospects look bright with that run under the belt and an extra 100m today. CROSSWAYS (1) is back after a 130-day spell. Was well in commission at both runs in the maiden prep in town but missed the placings each time. Produced a nice trial at Warwick Farm recently. This is a nice level to launch the new prep. SETESDAL (2) is a half-brother to classy sprinter Brudenell on debut. Went close in a recent Randwick trial so things look promising.",
